So `\p1` sets `drawing_scale = 1`. Then in `parse_events`, when `drawing_scale` is non-zero, it enters the drawing text parsing branch. If the drawing text is empty (e.g., `\p1` followed by `{` or end of string), then `drawing_text.len` would be 0.

But wait, let me check if `drawing_text.str` would be non-NULL even with len 0. Looking at the code:
```c
} else if (render_priv->state.drawing_scale) {
    q = p;
    if (*p == '{')
        q++;
    while ((*q != '{') && (*q != 0))
        q++;
    drawing_text.str = p;
    drawing_text.len = q - p;
    code = 0xfffc; // object replacement character
    p = q;
    break;
}
```

If `*p == '{'`, then `q = p + 1`, and `drawing_text.len = q - p = 1`. If `*p == 0` (end of string), then `q = p`, and `drawing_text.len = 0`. But wait, the outer while loop checks `while (*p)`, so `*p` is non-zero when entering this branch. So `*p` is not 0.

If `*p` is `{`, then `q = p + 1`, and `drawing_text.len = 1`. If `*p` is some other character, then `q` advances until `{` or 0, so `drawing_text.len >= 1`.

